coming highlighted (bg-primary/10 text-primary), clicking again 48→47 and unhighlighted. On GameMaster42's reply-1: 15→16 selected, click again →15 unselected, click again →16 selected — a single toggleable vote per user, updating immediately.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Search \\\"ZEBRA\\\" (uppercase) returned only \\\"QA Zebra Testing Thread\\\" (title match, case-insensitive). Search \\\"AUTOMATION checks\\\" matched only the same thread via its body text. Search \\\"xyzzyqwertynomatch\\\" returned 0 threads with clear feedback: 'Showing results for \\\"xyzzyqwertynomatch\\\"' + \\\"No threads found. Try adjusting your search terms.\\\"\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"/category/general lists only general threads (thread-2 \\\"Share your favorite productivity tips!\\\" + my new general thread). Switching to /category/tech changes the set to only tech threads (thread-7 mechanical keyboard, thread-1 programming language). Category title/description update accordingly.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"\\\"Most Active Discussions\\\" order by replies: 89, 67, 45, 41, 38, 34, 31, 24, 0, 0 — strictly descending. Threads A (thread-...508356) and B (thread-...677561) were both 0 replies with B listed above A; after posting one reply to A, A (1 reply) moved above B (0 replies), so the ranking updated with reply activity.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking thread.author on thread-1 opened /profile/user-1: \\\"TechExplorer\\\", \\\"Joined about 3 years ago\\\", \\\"2,450 reputation\\\", bio, interest tags (Programming/Open Source/AI-ML/DevOps) and authored threads (thread-1, thread-7). Clicking a reply author (reply-2 → NewsHound) opened /profile/user-5 with the same complete set incl. authored thread-6. (Minor anomaly: a freshly registered account shows \\\"Joined about 21 hours ago\\\" instead of just now.)\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After logging out and back in (no page reload): profile still shows bio \\\"QA engineer who loves testing forums.\\\" and interests Testing/Coffee/Hiking; both authored threads still listed on the profile; own reply \\\"Ranking test reply on thread A.\\\" and reply on thread-1 still present; vote state preserved and still shown as selected — thread A upvote = 1 (highlighted) and reply-1 upvote = 16 (highlighted).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-18\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No persistence across page reload — registered accounts and session are lost\", \"actual\": \"Registered qatester1@example.com and confirmed login worked before reload. After a page reload (navigating to /new-thread then /login), signing in with the exact same registered credentials was rejected — stayed on /login with logged-out nav (Sign up / Sign In), identical to the behavior for a never-registered email. The account no longer exists, so signed-in status, profile changes, threads, replies and votes cannot survive a reload either.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing/blank required fields are not identified — silent no-op\", \"actual\": \"Submitting the empty form and then a form with category \\\"General Discussion\\\" + whitespace-only title (\\\"   \\\") and whitespace-only content correctly created no discussion (stayed on /new-thread), but no missing information is identified: no error text in the form, no toast/[role=alert], no aria-invalid or required attributes on the title/content inputs. The user gets zero feedback about what is missing.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-17\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Password is not verified at sign-in\", \"actual\": \"Signed out, then signed in with qatester1@example.com and the incorrect password \\\"wrongpass123\\\" (registered password was \\\"passw0rd\\\"). Login succeeded: redirected to home and nav showed logged-in state (nav.profile = \\\"qatester1\\\", nav.logout present). No error message shown.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No sign-in screen for unauthenticated discussion creation; blank page\", \"actual\": \"While logged out there is no \\\"New Thread\\\" entry point in the UI at all (nav shows only Home/Login/Register). Opening the discussion-creation route /new-thread while unauthenticated renders a completely blank page (document.body.innerText === \\\"\\\", accessibility snapshot contains only an empty notifications region) — no redirect to login, no sign-in form, and therefore no way to return to discussion creation after authenticating.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"\\\"Trending Discussions\\\" order by upvotes: 156, 124, 92, 89, 78, 67, 56, 47, 0, 0 — strictly descending. Threads A and B were tied at 0 with B listed above A; after upvoting A, A (1 upvote) immediately moved above B (0), so the ranking updates with voting.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Displayed reply total does not match the replies actually listed\", \"actual\": \"thread-1 displays \\\"23 replies\\\" (list and detail view) but its detail view lists only 2 actual replies (reply-1, reply-2). After posting one reply the counter became \\\"24 replies\\\" while only 3 replies are listed. The seeded totals are fabricated, so the counter and the listed replies are inconsistent for every seeded thread.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No recent time window stated or applied for Trending / Most Active\", \"actual\": \"The Trending and Most Active views show only \\\"Trending Discussions\\\" / \\\"Most Active Discussions\\\" headings with the subtitle \\\"Join the conversation with our community\\\" — no time period (e.g. \\\"this week\\\", \\\"last 7 days\\\") is stated anywhere. Ranking uses lifetime totals: the top trending item is thread-6 posted \\\"over 2 years ago\\\" with 156 all-time upvotes, and every seeded thread (all 1-3 years old) is ranked purely on its cumulative upvote/reply counters, with no restriction to interactions in any recent window.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Category and community counts are hard-coded and do not reflect real records or updates\", \"actual\": \"Sidebar shows General Discussion (156), Technology (243), Creative Corner (89), Lifestyle (167), Gaming (312), News (78) but each category page lists only 1-2 actual threads (general = 2, tech = 2). Community stats show 1,045 threads / 4,823 replies / 892 members while the forum contains only 8 seeded threads and a handful of members. After registering a new member the members count stayed 892, and after publishing a new General Discussion thread both stats.threads (1,045) and the General Discussion category count (156) were unchanged.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
